---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageIntro from '../components/PageIntro.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Colophon"
  description="A small, static website built with Astro, TypeScript, and MDX, designed for readability, accessibility, and simple maintenance."
>
  <PageIntro
    label="Colophon"
    title="A small site, built with care."
    description="A few decisions behind the pages you’re reading."
  />
  <article class="prose colophon-prose">
    <h2>Content first</h2>
    <p>
      This site is built with Astro and strict TypeScript. Work, research, and
      lab entries live in schema-validated MDX collections, keeping the writing
      separate from the layouts.
    </p>
    <h2>Only the interaction that helps</h2>
    <p>
      Most pages are static HTML. A small React component powers the regression,
      classification, and evaluation workspace in the lab; its explanatory
      content and initial results remain readable without JavaScript.
    </p>
    <h2>Readable by design</h2>
    <p>
      The design uses system serif and sans-serif fonts, a quiet neutral
      palette, and a green accent. There are no external font requests, stock
      profile photographs, or decorative animations. Keyboard access, visible
      focus, contrast, and smaller screens are part of the design.
    </p>
    <h2>A quiet corner of the web</h2>
    <p>
      There are no analytics, tracking scripts, advertising, accounts, or
      third-party embeds. Contact links open email or an external professional
      profile.
    </p>
    <h2>Attribution & responsibility</h2>
    <p>
      Professional descriptions draw on my public profile. Research
      contributions link to their sources, and demonstrations are labeled as
      synthetic. Writing, identity, and third-party material are not offered
      under a blanket open-source license.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
